Scenario: View user on closed account
	Testing the ability to create a contact in Dossiera and viewing the respective user on a closed account in the provisioning user details page

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Usrkor - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | USR                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | USR                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki4                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Korusr - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I create a team with the name "User Site Partner" for the account "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I assign the team with the name "User Site Partner" on the account "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the team "User Site Partner"
	| usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default user customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Liferay User Customer Role                          |
	| Type        | Account Customer                                    |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Liferay User Customer Role |
	And I update a koroneiki account with the name "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}" to have the following values
	| Status | Closed | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticKoroneikiAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticKoroneikiAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the user index page
	And I search the users page using the keyword "usr.koroneiki1"
	Then I should be able to view a user on the provisioning index with the name "USR Koroneiki1" and the following values
	| Name               | USR Koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address      | usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Number of Accounts | 1                                    |
	| Status             | VERIFIED                             |
	When I click on the user with the name "USR Koroneiki1" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the following user values in the user details page
	| Name               | USR Koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address      | usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Number of Accounts | 1                                    |
	| Status             | VERIFIED                             |
	And I should be able to view the contact account with the name "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Name          | Korusr - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Code          | USRKORKORUSR                  |
